are not required\"; no datasets, no ML libraries (no torch/transformers/vllm), network disabled, 224 CPUs and no GPU flag \u2014 so the protocol is grounded in published conventions (GCG/AdvBench/refusal-judge) and no experiment was or can be run here.", "assumptions": ["\u2018Suffix length\u2019 = optimization-time token count; suffix content is re-optimized at each length so length is causal.", "Saturation is assessed on same-model white-box ASR on a frozen 100-prompt eval set; transfer saturation is out of scope.", "ASR is judged by a pre-registered local refusal classifier (binary); no external harmfulness APIs.", "A ~60\u201366 GPU-hour budget is assumed for a hypothetical future run; the design fits it via the 3-seed secondary model and forward-only controls.", "All GCG hyperparameters, seeds, sweep levels, judge rulebook, and tests are pre-registered constants, not tunables.", "The 50-token cap bounds the investigated regime; statements do not extend beyond L=50."], "uncertainties": ["Statistical power of the marginal-gain rule at n=100 prompts (CI width \u2248 \u00b110pp at ASR 0.5); mitigated by bootstrap pooling and the breakpoint/slope test, but acknowledged as a limitation.", "Whether the optional Llama-3-8B judge-agreement pass stays within \u22485% of budget; if not it is dropped and reported out-of-scope.", "Whether conclusions will converge across the two victims (reported either way).", "The plateau location is unknown a priori; the pre-registered finer-resolution sensitivity sweep is optional and conditional on the observed shape.", "Uniform-token random-suffix control is an upper-baseline, not a semantic baseline; a natural-text control was noted but not added to the primary grid."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-1a3f9f4cf5a143db8e1021773dbd2b9f", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Deliver full pre-registered protocol for adversarial suffix length vs ASR saturation design", "kind": "ActionEvent